Hi,

We received the attached IRS notice CP207 on October 29 for our Q2 2026 Form =
941. It proposes a deposit penalty of $4,534.32 and says our return showed mo=
nthly liabilities instead of a Schedule B. Please work out whether the penalt=
y is right and draft our reply. The notice is dated October 26, so we have 45=
 days.

Our payroll system deposits every regular payroll through EFTPS on the next b=
usiness day after the payday; the EFTPS history and the return as filed are a=
ttached, and the payroll by payday, our employer details and the IRS account =
history are in the folder.

Three things you should know:

- The June 26 off-cycle bonus run (PR-2614, paid with the regular payroll tha=
t day) is not in the system's automatic EFTPS batch, and I did not schedule i=
ts deposit. I caught it in the July reconciliation and made the deposit mysel=
f on July 7.
- The payroll system's upgrade on May 4 reset its Form 941 setting from semiw=
eekly to monthly. The Q1 return went in before that with a Schedule B; the Q2=
 return went in with the monthly box on line 16 and no Schedule B.
- The Q3 return is being prepared separately with a Schedule B. The setting i=
n the system still says monthly.

Thanks,
Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC

--=_HCS_2026_CP207_request
